licant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAYA HAYATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGOI, HISAO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHOWA DENKO K.K.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, JUN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAYA, HAYATO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOGOI HISAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA JUN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAYA HAYATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGOI, HISAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, JUN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAYA, HAYATO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Ultra-fine particles of zinc oxide which have a specific surface area of 10 to 200 m&lt;2&gt;/g as measured by one point BET method, have primary particles being substantially isotropic with respect to the form thereof, characterized in that it has a specific volume of 4 to 40 ml/g as measured by means of a tapping machine; a method for preparing the same; and a cosmetic comprising the same. The ultra-fine particles have a reduced degree of aggregation of primary particles and thus can be extremely easily dispersed into and suspended in an aqueous solvent with no pulverization steps or through a simple dry pulverization, can be suitably used, for example, as a powder for a cosmetic, and further have both of feeling of transparency and ultraviolet ray-shielding function.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des particules d'oxyde de zinc ultra-fines présentant une aire spécifique de 10 à 200 m&lt;2&gt;/g mesurée par la méthode BET à un point. Ces particules sont constituées de particules primaires sensiblement isotropes par rapport à leur forme, et se caractérisent par un volume de 4 à 40 ml/g mesuré par une machine à choc. L'invention concerne également un procédé de préparation desdites particules et un produit cosmétique les contenant. Les  particules ultra-fines présentent un niveau d'agrégation des particules primaires réduit et peuvent donc être dispersées en suspension très facilement dans un solvant aqueux, sans passer par une étape de pulvérisation, ou par simple pulvérisation à sec. Les  particules peuvent être utilisées de manière appropriée, par exemple, comme poudre destinée à un produit cosmétique, et présentent en outre à la fois un aspect transparent et une fonction de protection contre les rayons ultraviolets.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>